course: dictionary
lesson: 15060
title: Reverting: going back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Reverting means going back to something you were or did before. It comes from the verb revert, and reverting is the -ing form, which shows it is happening now. «Sam is reverting to his old messy spelling over the holidays.» The word tells you Sam is going back to spelling he used before, not learning something new.
explain: Reverting often goes with the words «reverting to» or «reverting back». Look at what comes after it. In «The family is reverting to their old habits», the old habits are the way they are going back to. Ask yourself: is something going back to how it was before? If yes, reverting fits.
explain: Computers use the word too. «The teacher is reverting the document to the version from Monday» means she is undoing the changes and getting back the earlier version. The context tells you which meaning is right: a person, a habit, a document, or an animal.
fact: Reverting means going back to an earlier state, habit or way of behaving.
fact: «Reverting» is the -ing form of the verb «revert», so it describes something happening now.
fact: In law, reverting means property going back to its former owner.
fact: In computing, reverting means undoing changes and returning to an earlier version.
fact: In science, wild-bred animals or plants can be reverting to their wild form.
exercise: «Sam is reverting to his old messy spelling over the holidays.» What is Sam doing? | Learning a brand new language | Writing a letter to his grandad | *Going back to an old habit | Winning a spelling bee
exercise: A teacher says, «I am reverting the document to the version from Monday.» What is she doing? | Painting a picture of the school | *Undoing changes to get back an earlier version | Deleting the whole school website | Making a brand new copy
exercise: Find the word that is the -ing form of revert: «The team is reverting back to the plan they had before.» | plan | team | *reverting | before
test: «After the storm, the garden is reverting to wild grass.» What does reverting mean here? | Being painted green | Being tidied up with new plants | Growing very tall in one day | *Going back to an earlier, wild state
test: Ella says reverting and changing mean the same thing. Which is true? | Reverting means shouting very loudly | *Reverting means going back to how something was before | Reverting means moving forward into something completely new | Reverting means eating your dinner quickly
exam: Which sentence shows someone going back to an old habit? | Tom is learning to ride a bike for the first time | Tom is reading a book about space | *Tom is reverting to biting his nails, which he had stopped last year | Tom is painting the fence blue
